  "resolution": "Diagnosed the user's detached-door JSON: the panel was a correct ~0.125m (2/16) thick shell (9 outer + 9 reversed inner caps + walls, pivot seated), but it carried junk faces — outer loop [3,4,5,2,1,1] with corner 1 doubled, its inner mirror, and a fully degenerate wall [1,1,17,17]. Root cause was a malformed pentagon in the car BODY: a 5-gon stored as a 6-loop with a repeated last corner (a zero-length edge from an earlier loop-cut/create-face). detach copied it verbatim, and solidifyFaces counted that zero-length edge as a silhouette edge and spun a degenerate rim wall off it. Fix: added cleanLoop (strips consecutive + wrap-around repeated corners, keeps per-corner uv in lockstep); subMeshFromFaces now sanitizes every extracted loop and drops faces that collapse below a triangle; solidifyFaces also cleans inner-cap loops and skips a==b edges so it is robust when used standalone. The shell geometry is unchanged otherwise — just no zero-area slivers. New regression test (req_1222) feeds a doubled-corner face through detach and asserts no surviving repeated corner or zero-length edge; editMesh suite 72/72 green. Note: the body's malformed face was in the door selection so deleteFaces already removed it; other malformed faces elsewhere would want a general weld/clean pass, a separate future tool.",
